Description: Start no application whose GPU cannot be applied
 When the Graphics page's resolver, sparky-stereo-gpu-env, says that the GPU
 the person chose for an application cannot be used (exit status 4), the
 application is not started on another GPU: the launch fails through KIO's
 own launch-failure path (KProcessRunner's error, the ApplicationLauncherJob's
 errorText, shown by its UI delegate) with the program's name and the
 resolver's own words, what failed, why and what to do. The resolver keeps
 the problem and notifies it with a "Use NAME" choice for each GPU that can
 draw. A resolver that fails, crashes, cannot be started or does not answer
 within five seconds (longer than its own three-second wait for
 power-profiles-daemon) is said the same way, and the application is not
 started either. Automatic is a rule, not the person's choice: when it
 cannot place the application now (exit status 5, a browser while the power
 profile cannot be read), the application starts as the session would, as
 before, and the resolver has said and kept why. Without the resolver, or
 with its answer (exit status 0), nothing changes. A D-Bus activatable
 application is neither activated nor started when its GPU cannot be applied.
 Tests: shouldNotStartWhereItsGpuCannotBeUsed (six rows),
 shouldRunOnTheGpuOfTheGraphicsSettings (automatic_cannot_place) and
 shouldStartAnActivatableApplicationOnItsGpu (its_gpu_cannot_be_used).
Author: Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed, edition-only (the resolver is Sparky Stereo OS's Graphics page)
Last-Update: 2026-11-02

